.\" the regions between the markers, which tools/mangen rewrites from the
.\" word's help text (make generate).
.TH KARVI-DAEMON 1 "" "karvi"
.\" Paths and options are not hyphenated, and lines are not stretched.
.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
karvi\-daemon \- manage the private per\-user daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED SYNOPSIS: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon start\fR [\-\-foreground]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon stop\fR [\-\-grace | \-\-after=DURATION | \-\-force]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon restart\fR [\-\-grace | \-\-after=DURATION | \-\-force]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon status\fR [\-\-format text|json]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBdaemon serve\fR
.\" END GENERATED SYNOPSIS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" BEGIN GENERATED DESCRIPTION: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
.PP
Without an option, stop and restart refuse while the daemon reports active
jobs. \-\-grace drains the daemon, of any version or build, so that it rejects
new jobs and exits after the last it holds, and waits for it to exit.
\-\-after=DURATION drains and waits until the daemon exits or DURATION elapses,
whichever comes first, then forces the stop. \-\-force stops at once; unfinished
work still receives terminal records. Interrupting a wait ends the wait alone:
the daemon finishes its jobs and exits. \-\-help shows this text. Specified, not
yet available: daemon start \-\-start\-timeout DURATION.
.PP
A daemon serves the clients of its own build: its IPC schema and its build,
the Go build ID's last part that karvi version names, both equal the client's;
status shows each of the daemon's values over the client's. A submission (run,
crun, a stream's job) and daemon start drain a daemon of another build, killing
nothing: one holding no job exits and is replaced in the same invocation, and
one with jobs finishes them and exits, every submission refused until then
(daemon_draining). job follow and job cancel reach a daemon of any build at
the client's IPC schema. Status, stop, restart, and the drain reach a daemon of
an older IPC schema at its own; one of a newer schema is stopped with the newer
karvi.
.PP
Under daemon.launch = "systemd" the daemon is the unit
karvi\-daemon@USER.service's, USER the client's own account (karvi\-sysutil(8)
installs it), which no client drains or starts: a daemon of another build, or
none, refuses a submission and daemon start, naming systemctl restart or start
of the unit, and stop and restart are refused (daemon_managed).
.\" END GENERATED DESCRIPTION
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR BASEDIR/socket/d.sock ", " BASEDIR/socket/c.sock
The daemon's socket and the credential channel's, the operator's alone, in
the socket directory
.RB ( daemon.sockets ,
at most 100 bytes).
.TP
.IR BASEDIR/state/daemon.json ", " BASEDIR/logs/daemon.log
Its state and its log.
.PP
A job runs under the configuration of the client that submitted it, sent in
its plan; the daemon's own configuration, its launching invocation's, serves
the process alone: the
.B daemon.*\&
keys, the
.B basedir
of its socket, state, and log, and the sweeps at its start.
A key whose reload class is
.B daemon\-start
reaches a running daemon at its next start.
.PP
A daemon a client launched passes on a filtered environment:
.BR HOME ,
.BR USER ,
.BR LOGNAME ,
.BR PATH ,
the names in
.BR security.child\-environment\-allowlist ,
every
.B KARVI__
variable,
.BR KARVI_ASKPASS_PATH ,
.BR TZ ,
and
.BR TMPDIR ,
so
.B NETPASS
never reaches it; the client resolves credentials and hands them over per
job.
After
.B daemon.shutdown\-idle\-timer
(10m) with no job and no request but a status, the daemon stops itself,
exit 0, with a
.B stopping: idle
line in its log, and the next run launches another; 0 never stops.
The service account's unit runs it with the timer at 0, since
.B Restart=on\-failure
does not restart a clean exit.
.PP
A drained daemon admits no job, finishes those it holds, and exits after the
last, exit 0, with a
.B stopping: drained
line in its log; a run of another build drains an operator's daemon so and,
when it holds no job, starts one of its own build at once.
.PP
The service account's daemon runs under the template unit
.BR karvi\-daemon@.service ,
the package's or the bundle's,
as
.BR karvi\-daemon@karvi.service ,
which
.BR karvi\-sysutil (8)
sets up with
.B daemon.launch = \(dqsystemd\(dq
in the account's configuration: its client neither drains nor starts a
daemon, and
.B daemon stop
and
.B daemon restart
are refused, naming
.BR systemctl .
The unit signals the daemon alone at a stop
.RB ( KillMode=mixed )
and leaves the bound to the daemon's grace
.RB ( TimeoutStopSec=infinity ).
After an upgrade the administrator's
.B systemctl restart karvi\-daemon@karvi.service
drains the old daemon and starts the installed one.
.SH SEE ALSO
